  "slug": "visualization-gfaidx-7f7d",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and a publication add fast GFA indexing, editable RNA structure figures, and batch motif visualization in PyMOL.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is tooling that makes large or structurally complex biological data inspectable and reusable through visualization. In genome graph analysis, gfaidx indexes GFA graphs for low-memory retrieval of gene-sized subgraphs and haplotypes, and gfaidx-viz extends this to visualization; the preprint reports speedups over ODGI and vg exceeding 100-fold. For RNA, AptaRender provides a browser-based, dependency-free editor that converts DNA/RNA sequences and dot-bracket structures into interactive, editable 2D SVG or PNG figures. RSMViewer, a published open-source PyMOL plugin, supports batch visualization and superimposition of RNA structural motif instances. The domains differ: the genome graph work addresses retrieval efficiency, while the RNA tools address figure generation and motif comparison. The new contribution across these reports is pairing scalable data access or structural comparison with interactive, reproducible rendering.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
